report=['# M0 architecture and route audit','', '**Static audit complete. Final architecture proposed; beta integration is not implemented or qualified by this report.**','', '## Main decision','', 'Use a Native98-derived Android shell and shared native flight/payload dispatch for the final beta. Reuse mission92/offline94 portable document/parser/compiler at its boundary; adapt Workbench planning/analysis, BetaVideo03 media and SIM-STABILITY03 physics/lifecycle/manual behavior through explicit contracts. Keep the original applications frozen and available as reference cases, but do not select multiple flight writers in one run.','', 'MissionBeta01 is a useful actual AUTO/workflow baseline, but its Android Activity only brokers host pages/workspaces/SAF. The host owns the live MissionLink. This differs materially from the final controller goal and must be stated rather than treating both as equivalent native flight implementations.','', '## Source-backed paths','']
for r in routes:report+=['- **'+r['id']+'**: '+' → '.join(r['path'])+'. Evidence '+', '.join(r['references'])+'.']
report+=['','## Retain/adapt/retire decisions','','| ID | Area | Decision | Selection and required repair |','|---|---|---|---|']
for d in decisions:report.append('| '+d['id']+' | '+d['area']+' | '+d['decision']+' | '+d['selected']+'. '+d['workRequired']+' |')
report+=['','## Blocking seams, not finished functions','']
for b in blockers:report+=['- **'+b['id']+' / '+b['severity']+'**: '+b['title']+'. '+b['resolution']+' (refs '+', '.join(b['evidence'])+').']
report+=['','## Smallest coherent assembly','','1. New native beta shell loads a single packaged origin and one selected controller; it retains native durable storage/SAF and direct-flight policy modules.','2. A FlightProvider descriptor binds AP artifact/config/model/endpoint and fresh session/boot identity. Existing ranchu/localhost/binary guards remain in legacy source; replacements live only in a new version with equivalent or stricter validation.','3. The final host simulator runs AP/FDM, sensor/camera peers, recorder, fault proxy, ground-truth observer and media. It does not expose a concurrently selected host flight-write controller.','4. Native-selected dispatch remains the only flight intent writer. Independent B submits only scoped payload intent through an authenticated, versioned ingress; global per-resource ownership must be implemented and verified, not inferred from local Native98 lease state. Broker deployment can migrate to controller/onboard hardware later without changing domain contract.','5. Workbench functions produce/inspect one selected mission document; a single presenter owns each Plan/Preflight/Fly/Review surface. Native92 vs Workbench workspace schema conversion is explicit and tested. No runtime string replacement becomes an undocumented product dependency.','6. Media source/decoder/clock/trace remain separate from flight throughput. Observer graphics/audio never control aircraft and never count as camera exposure.','', 'M1 may preserve the proven host-manual path as an explicitly reference-only harness while recorder/lifecycle regressions are repaired. Passing that harness will not qualify the new final native provider. The ported native/manual path needs its own Android/AP gate.','', '## Evidence index','']
for r in refs:report.append('- '+r['id']+': `'+r['path']+':'+str(r['line'])+'` — '+r['observation'])
report+=['','## Limits and integrity','',f'Read {len(inputs)} existing files and recorded {len(refs)} source references. Every input SHA was rechecked before writing the report. No product module was imported or executed, no endpoint connected, and no source/candidate/ENDURE path changed. Reports are written only under the assigned new M0 architecture scopes. This is an architectural recommendation and static evidence, not runtime PASS, complete dependency closure, hardware integration or human/flight acceptance.','']
(P/'REPORT.md').open('x').write('\n'.join(report))
